From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:31:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] fix(registry): serialize shared sqlite connection access
 (R-1)

All SQLiteRegistry methods ran on asyncio.to_thread worker threads against one
shared sqlite3 connection without a lock. Interleaved transactions let a failing
writer's rollback discard another writer's uncommitted insert, so creates were
reported as successful but never persisted, and raw sqlite3 errors leaked.

Serialize every database call through an instance-level RLock.
